COMMAND NAME: mppdeletecluster.sh

Deletes a Greenplum database system that was initialized using mppcreatecluster.sh.


*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppdeletecluster.sh -d <data_directory> [-f] [-r] [-l <logfile_directory>]

mppdeletecluster.sh [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppdeletecluster.sh script will perform the following actions:

* Stop all postmaster processes (the segment instances and MPP master 
  instance).

* Delete all data directories.

Before runing this script, you should move any backup files (created by 
mpp_dump) out of the master and segment data directories.

This script will not uninstall the Greenplum database software.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-d <data_directory>

Required. The MPP master host data directory.

-f

Force a delete even if backup files are found in the data directories. The 
default is to not delete Greenplum database instances if backup files (created 
by mpp_dump) are present.

-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Delete a Greenplum database system:

mppdeletecluster.sh -d /mppdata/mpp0


Delete a Greenplum database system even if backup files are present:

mppdeletecluster.sh -d /mppdata/mpp0 -f


